  "findings": [
    "Throughput peaks at 8 concurrent files; beyond that, latency grows with the queue (Little's law: at 64 files, 256 requests in flight at 9.4 chunks/s predicts about 27 s; median 21.6 s).",
    "The server answered no request with 429 at any point: its admission limits (queue 512) were not reached.",
    "At 128 files, Windows refused connections to the forwarded port (WinError 10061) for 270 attempts (205 in the repeat); every request that reached the app succeeded and the app logged no error. 512 simultaneous short uploads passed both through port forwarding and inside the Docker network, so the refusals need many long-lived forwarded connections."
  ]
